      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>This paraphrase of the second half of Psalms 19 in English verse by Sir Robert Grant was first published posthumously under the title “Psalm XIX” by Robert’s brother Charles Grant (Lord Glenelg) in <tei:hi rend="italic">Sacred Poems by the Late Right Hon. Sir Robert Grant</tei:hi> (1839), pp. 28-30. As Charles Grant writes as introduction to the poem, it “is intended as a sequel or counterpart to [Joseph] Addison’s hymn, “The spacious firmament.” It corresponds to the latter portion of the 19th Psalm, as Addison’s does to the former.”</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_66980_notes"/>
